					}
				],
				"max_completion_tokens": 2048
			},
			"output": {
				"text": "KV caching stores the key and value tensors computed at each layer during the autoregressive generation of a transformer so that, on the next token prediction, the model only needs to compute attention for the new token against the cached keys and values rather than reprocessing the entire sequence from scratch. This avoids redundant computation across decoding steps, reducing time complexity from O(n\u00b2) to O(n) per new token and making text generation significantly faster."
			},
